WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.943
Before we build a model, let's understand the ideas behind it.

2
00:00:04.943 --> 00:00:10.217
In this lesson, you will learn why we connect tables, the four kinds of

3
00:00:10.217 --> 00:00:14.737
cardinality, how filters flow, and the difference between dimension and fact tables.

4
00:00:14.737 --> 00:00:16.620
Let's get the basics right!

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.509
On this report page, I wrote the key ideas as notes.

6
00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:27.611
A relationship joins one table with another, so we can work with them as

7
00:00:27.611 --> 00:00:29.069
if they were one.

8
00:00:29.069 --> 00:00:31.620
It reduces repeated data, and connects everything.

9
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.820
Cardinality describes how many matching values each side has. One to one:

10
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.220
both tables have one instance of each value. Many to one:

11
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.020
one table repeats the value many times.

12
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.420
One to many is the opposite.

13
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.020
And many to many:

14
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.620
both tables repeat values.

15
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.352
In Model view, Products and Order Details show many to one.

16
00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:09.100
Each product appears once in Products, but many times in Order Details.

17
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:15.900
Manage relationships lists every link, with its tables, columns, and status: active or inactive.

18
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.471
Cross filter direction decides how filters travel.

19
00:01:19.471 --> 00:01:22.643
Both means filters work in both directions.

20
00:01:22.643 --> 00:01:26.720
Single means filters only flow from the dimension table.

21
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.447
There are two kinds of tables.

22
00:01:29.447 --> 00:01:30.998
Dimension tables describe things:

23
00:01:30.998 --> 00:01:33.325
who, what, when, where, and why.

24
00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:36.040
Fact tables hold the numbers: what happened.

25
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.960
To see a relationship in action, I add table visuals:

26
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.920
product IDs from one table, and region names from another.

27
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.356
Then I add a text box to label each visual, so readers understand what

28
00:02:27.356 --> 00:02:28.600
they are looking at.

29
00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.233
Back in Model view, here is the full model:

30
00:02:46.233 --> 00:02:48.388
customers, orders, products, regions, and more.

31
00:02:48.388 --> 00:02:51.980
In the next lessons, we connect them step by step.

